Based on the Wireshark network logs, the network interruption was caused by aDenial of Service (DoS) SYN Flood attack originating from a single source IP address: 203.0.113.0

Log analysis -- 3.01 - 51.06 seconds

– The logs show Normal traffic at first (logs 47-49) an employee browser established a 3 way handshake and as a result, HTTPS connection (logs 50,51).
– We see the suspect IP address makes a proper 3 way handshake. (logs 52-54) No HTTPS follows.
– logs 61, 64 show only two steps of a three-way handshake SYN & server answers the suspect IP with SYN, ACK but gets no ACK from, Bad actor holds half open connections.
–TCP backlog queue becomes saturated. The server begins dropping connections:
log 73 – RST, ACK -  reset, connection attempt dropped by the web server. log 77 – server gateway timeout.

Analysis of the packet capture confirms a single-source DOS SYN flood attack originating from 203.0.113.0.
logs 125 - 214 shows the server stops responding and the logs show only the malicious actor sending SYN packets.


A three-way handshake:
1. The first step – 
The client (website visitor) sends a request to the server in order to connect or “synchronize”. This is a SYN packet. 

2. The second step – 
The web server sends the same client a SYN, ACK. meaning the web server “acknowledges” synchronize (step 1),
an acceptance to connection and reserves resources in its memory TCP backlog queue.

3. The client then sends an ACK packet which is the third and last step, meaning the visitor tells the web server it confirms the connection.


When a malicious actor sends a large number of SYN packets all at once, the server sends back SYN, ACK, and reserves some resources for the client to connect at first, 
waiting for an ACK from the client - A half-open connection.
Instead of confirming connection (ACK), all of the incoming SYN packets overwhelm the server & website server becomes exhausted & unable to respond to requests.

Once resources were depleted, the server could no longer process new requests, causing it to drop legitimate connections and malfunction. 
logs 73, 77, 80 and so on…  [RST, ACK]. 
server stops connections eventually completely.

